Another known solution:
```
def total(basket):
    counts = [basket.count(i) for i in range(1,6)]
    counts.sort(reverse=True)
    groups = [0]*6
    while counts[0] > 0:
        size = sum(1 for c in counts if c > 0)
        groups[size] += 1
        counts = [c-1 if c > 0 else 0 for c in counts]
        counts.sort(reverse=True)
    while groups[5] and groups[3]:
        groups[5] -= 1
        groups[3] -= 1
        groups[4] += 2
    return sum(groups[i] * prices[i] for i in range(1,6)) / 100
```
